---
<Title id="case-title">Care Outreach<br><em>Automation.</em></Title><p class="dialog-lead">From researched spreadsheet to tracked outreach and personalised proposals.</p><SectionTitle>The problem</SectionTitle><p>Lead files, company history, campaign details and Gmail conversations can become disconnected. Sending more messages alone doesn’t solve that.</p><SectionTitle>What I built</SectionTitle><ol><li><strong>Research intake:</strong> normalises uploaded Excel data and brings providers into shared records.</li><li><strong>Company checks:</strong> compares identities and contact history across campaigns, and records published email evidence.</li><li><strong>Outreach coordination:</strong> queues personalised messages and follow-ups within daily budgets and UK sending windows.</li><li><strong>Reply monitoring:</strong> checks six connected inboxes, classifies consultancy replies and suppresses follow-ups after interest or opt-outs.</li><li><strong>Requested proposals:</strong> generates a branded eight-page PDF with approved plans and prices when a brief is explicitly requested.</li></ol><SectionTitle>Built with boundaries</SectionTitle><p>Published email evidence does not prove mailbox deliverability. Preliminary care-service matching does not prove tender eligibility. The system records those distinctions instead of treating every imported row as ready to send.</p><SectionTitle>What this portfolio demonstrates</SectionTitle><p>The interactive walkthrough uses fictional data. Edited workflow recordings are available on the full case study. Public workflow exports are not included. No live inbox or outreach queue is connected to this website.</p><a class="button" href={inDialog ? "#contact" : "/#contact"} id={inDialog ? "case-contact" : undefined}>Discuss a similar project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>